"""Studio Stage 0: root-candidate teacher consistency eval (second dispatch).

Why positions are generated, not read from ds_m3s2: evaluate_root needs a
live FastCarbon state (it clones the sim from a full observation), and
ds_m3s2 samples are one-way encoded features -- a sim state cannot be
reconstructed from them. So, exactly like stage0_measure_teacher.py,
positions are harvested from bare-net self-play games (m3s2r1 vs itself,
temp 1.0 sampling) at steps 40..240. At each sampled step we also record
the joint action the bare net actually sampled for the `me` seat.

Per position, stage0_teacher.evaluate_root (K=16, M=8, H=2, teacher=1):
  - agree_greedy: teacher argmax(q) == greedy arm (internal, exact)
  - entropy of the target q
  - teacher-top arm labels vs the actually-sampled joint action:
    exact joint match + per-slot match (arms recovered by re-running the
    deterministic gen_candidates on the same inputs)
Cost: wall ms per position + extrapolation to 35,282 positions (ds_m3s2
sample count) for the record.

Run from code/ with:
  env -u CNET2_TEMP_KIND CNET2_TEACHER=1 \
    python3 stage0_teacher_consistency_studio.py <npz> [max_seconds] [max_games]
Prints one JSON line per position + a CONSISTENCY summary line.
"""
import copy
import json
import os
import sys
import time
import types

import numpy as np

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, HERE)

